# Cut record — chain 21 (docs/deploy.md, "Cut policy"; audit v6, OPS-7). DRAFT, 2026-10-12.
#
# Drafted from deploy/cut-record.template by the cutover-prep session; NOT published, NOT final.
# Every `TODO(user…)` is a field only the user (or the second operator) can fill. While any of
# reason/carries/drops/clients/second-operator/rollback starts with TODO, deploy/cut-chain21-genesis.sh
# refuses the cut (`require_cut_record`), and while `second-hash:` is empty or another hash,
# deploy/cutover-fleet-chain21.sh push refuses (`require_second_rebuild`). Runbook:
# docs/chain21-cut-runbook.md. Lines starting with # are ignored; one line per field.

chain-id: 21

reason: v0.8.0 runs chain 21 onward only — constraint set 9 (rVM phase 4's Merkle spans and the MODQ chip) changes every verifier key and the proof encoding, so v0.8.0 refuses chains 18–20 at startup and no rolling update can carry it; and chain 21's genesis-gated rules need a new genesis: the `fees` section (burn_base + burn_floor), the `perps` section (RPL-3, BTC-PERP on zUSD, engine_hc f286a611…1573), the `multisig` section seeding the foundation treasury (2 of 3, new issuance), and private multisig — the genesis field hc_auth_multisig = 9705f8e2f1bc8561848b29cb8efd57c37e3e39788fa58a5f03304d8019668247 with max_proof_bytes 6291456 (6 MiB) and max_block_bytes 19922944 (19 MiB), cut WITH the field although no multisig-private spend has ever been proven (the user's decision, 2026-10-12; see the runbook's known risk).

carries: the 26 validators × 1 000 RAND on chain 20's keys (same peer ids, same hosts — the current droplets); the bridge state from the chain-20 snapshot at height 814702 (2026-10-12T07:41:55Z, bridge stopped 07:40–07:41Z): guardian set 1, burn_sequence 14, inbound floors from the endpoints' next sequences {2: 3, 3: 5, 4: 3, 5: 7} (never below chain 20's {2: 3, 3: 3, 4: 3, 5: 7}; the relayer's done/ agrees on every chain), chain 20's emitters unchanged, bridge.rotation and bridge.fees 10/10 bps to fingerprint 89DS-4Q4X-HXSX-MBYW; locked ETH-USDT 22 / BSC-USDT 23.001999 / Tron-USDT 30 / Sol-USDT 25 = 100.001999 == custody; 100.001999 zUSD as three genesis notes per ZUSD_CARRY (anish 10, the owner's wallet 89DS-4Q4X-HXSX-MBYW 89.002999 = 89 carried + the bridge's 10 bps fees on the two BNB mints and the one burn since chain 20's genesis, shielded-5 0.999 found by the balances scan); 3 938.879078887 RAND as genesis allocs to the seven operator wallets the balances scan found (balances.json heights 822056..822229, chain 20 still running) (relayer 299.977, shielded-1 194.992, -2 674.996, -3 879.983, -4 839.998, -5 989.937, docs-programs 58.996078887; every note store rescanned from leaf 0 against obs1 / rand-archive-2 on 2026-10-12 09:21–10:05Z — nine stores in parallel, then the balances step with BALANCES_RESCAN=0 resuming those stores, so the cut prints the not-rescanned warning although each store rests on the chain alone); NEW ISSUANCE (not carried): the multisig treasury, 2 of 3 signers (treasury-1, -2, -3 from ~/.rand-chain21/treasury.txt), 100 000 RAND, create_fee 1 RAND; hc_auth_multisig (private multisig) as above; perps genesis_root da0e3a53d93e50ec03fa40c6d2bd3dad8b9c7b4f542175e86a1dea567cbb9846 (the perp-prover dry run; the cut re-derives it).

drops: ≈ 36 025.026027822 RAND of chain 20's shielded pool: the pool held 39 963.905106709 RAND at height 814703 and the operator wallets 3 938.879078887 — the rest is held by wallets the operator does not hold (35 040 RAND of faucet mints to the allow-list's recipients, payments made to users), whose notes cannot be re-created without their addresses; 2.606397841 RAND of validator fee rewards not withdrawn (23 of the 26 validators; REWARDS_DROPPED_OK=1 as at chain 20); no zUSD (Σ carried == Σ locked == custody); the 11 other tokens registered on chain 20 (ALLOW_DROPPED_TOKENS=1, confirmed by the user 2026-10-12): DUR Durian (supply 1 000 000 000, 6 dec, durian.market's chain-20 token), RDLP durian.market RAND/DUR LP (63 245.552203), PERPLP perp LP (9), EXT Example Token (1 000), EXF Example Fixed (1 000), EXM Example Mintable (145), AMMLP AMM share (8.999999), CFR Crowdfund receipt (3), SSLP StableSwap share (3.499999), LEND Lending share (3.999999), RUSD RAND-backed stable (0) — all registered in chain 20's first hours by the docs/program examples and durian.market, none bridge-backed; their notes and the programs' state are not carried (durian.market is rebuilt against v0.8.0 after the cut and re-registers what it needs).

clients: rand CLI v0.8.0 (tag v0.8.0 at fullnode c0878c3f, the release asset, signed SHA256SUMS; wallet `rand multisig-private …` for private multisig, the auth proof proved locally at tier 18); bridge relayer: the Linux v0.8.0 `rand` from the same release, installed on rand-relayer-1 at the switch (the bridge steps); clients repo: main vendors a pre-private-multisig fullnode and its proofs do not decode on chain 21 (constraint set 9) — the chain-21 wallets are clients PR #3 (feat/msauth-signing, vendors fullnode v0.8.0 c0878c3, all platforms' tests green) and are NOT released at the cut; chain-20 wallets stay on clients release/chain20; the apps' default RPC host is still chain 20's; randscan main 60d5612 and randbridge.org 9b395f8 are v0.8.0-compatible (deploy needs randscan migration 014); website WASM / durian.market: NOT rebuilt before the cut — the cut goes ahead without them, and both are rebuilt against v0.8.0 right after it (the user's decision, 2026-10-12); accepted for this cut: the website's in-browser wallet and durian.market cannot prove on chain 21 until those rebuilds land.

second-operator: WAIVED — the user's decision in the executing session, 2026-10-12 (as at chain 20: one operator holds every validator key and every host; Anish Mohammed was named but was not standing by, and the genesis clock starts at the cut). cutover-fleet-chain21.sh push runs with SECOND_REBUILD_WAIVED=1 and appends `second-rebuild-waived:` below.

# Filled by the second operator after their rebuild: `rand-node init --datadir <tmp> --genesis
# genesis-chain21.json` with the v0.8.0 release rand-node on their own machine; the cutover's push
# compares it with the author's hash (`require_second_rebuild`) and refuses on a mismatch or a blank.
second-hash:

rollback: every host keeps chain 20's data dir (-6210cf07…, data-20 on the guardian hosts) and the v0.7.0 binaries (what chain 20 runs: 0.7.0, git_sha 806ed349) as /root/rand-node.pre-c21 and /root/rand.pre-c21 (sha-checked against v0.7.0's signed SHA256SUMS) for at least a day, and the relayer (rand-relayer-1, 203.0.113.28) keeps its rand 0.6.8 (sha256 155dfe6667a85ea8071977512dc40c750127b9baa9b4fa4796d101c8fc1eee2d) as /usr/local/bin/rand.pre-c21, checked against that sha; the steps, in order: the bridge session stops the relayer and all eight guardians FIRST (deploy/chain21-bridge-steps.md); `deploy/cutover-fleet-chain21.sh quiet <genesis>` confirms nothing was burned or minted on chain 21 (else the user decides: a rollback loses it); `halt`, `rollback` (units/drop-ins and binaries restored), `start`, `wait20` (all 26 on chain 20 and C's height moving); then the bridge's chain-20 configs, cursors and the relayer's 0.6.8 rand (sha-checked) are restored and the daemons started; retire-chain-dirs.sh is not run until chain 21 has run a day.

